  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); fund balance 773,731 -> 443,658. Ending cash = printed Cash and cash equivalents 442,058 (p4); county treasurer cash 1,600 printed separately (not summed); no beginning cash printed. Transfers: General out 17,328, Street in 17,328; the Total column prints '-', so transfers_in/out are null (as in later years); per-fund transfers kept in detail. Capital outlay 406,847 (General 27,418 + Street 379,429) has no single printed function, labelled plain Capital Outlay. Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary statement Total column (p7), which ties to the Statement of Activities (Water 171,260, Sewer 52,215 expenses = 223,475; charges for services Water 94,598 includes 'Other revenue' 7,239). Business-type net position / cash at September 30, 2021 printed as '-' (p7, p8). Business-type receipts total computed (operating 179,093 + grant income 11,250); disbursements total 223,475 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Proprietary cash flow statement printed (p8: operating 41,429, capital and related financing -74,561) but proprietary left null as in later years (non-GAAP). General Fund budget 'General government' 118,669 includes capital outlay 27,418. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (p4; totals 443,658 equal the government-wide governmental column p1), business-type from p6; totals from p1 Total column. Budget schedules only for General and Street funds; no Water/Sewer detail (as in FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
